We are passing **"BATCH_MANUAL"** and **"BATCH_ASYNC"** as the changeType! The database sees "BATCH_MANUAL", realizes it isn't "ADD", "UPDATE", or "DELETE", and immediately throws the 409 Constraint Violation error, rolling back your entire transaction!
Here is the exact fix. We just need to update the logAudit calls in your backend to pass "ADD" or "DELETE" to satisfy the database constraint.
